    "norm": "An element selector may contain CSS-escaped special characters (a backslash followed by the literal character). {@link TokenQueue#consumeElementSelector()} should strip the escaping backslash and return the literal character as part of the tag name. <p>The queue below holds four space-separated, escaped selectors. Note the Java-source escaping: {@code \"\\\\\\\\\"} is the two characters {@code \\\\}, and {@code \"\\\\.\"} is the two characters {@code \\.}, so the queue effectively contains: {@code p\\\\p p\\.p p\\:p p\\!p}.</p>"
